CiukiOS fx-14: document admission against the memory actually available to
the browser, replacing the f6-14 amendment-1 constants that rejected ordinary
pages (T23 trial e831e685: http://www.google.com and https://www.bbc.co.uk/news
downloaded, then "NetSurf structure rejected: parser admission limit." and the
out-of-memory error page). The libdom hubbub binding charges every node and
attribute (CIUKI_DOM_NODE_BYTES plus its string bytes) against a budget of a
quarter of the free memory (sdk/netsurf/port/docmem.h; CiukiOS call 70,
host model of the 128 MiB baseline); the box tree, its layout splits and
plain text use the same share. No node-count, per-chunk or per-run cap below
the budget; script element text is dropped (no JavaScript here). DOM depth
64 -> 128, box depth 64 -> 256 (1 MiB main stack), table columns 64 -> 1000
with colspan clamped to 1000 as HTML specifies. Refused pages get an error
page that says why ("too large for the memory available to the browser",
nesting, columns). Bitmaps: 1024x1024 pixels in any shape up to 4096 wide or
high; GIF frame records 64 -> 1024 (charged to the image ledger).
Evidence: build/codex/fx-14-report.md, tests/host/netsurf.

